  "rationale": "No single non-foothold step is a chokepoint, because each one leaves at least one route to crownData:exfiltrate.\n\nThe target is an OR over vaultRead, mailArchive, codeRepo and shareMount. That gives several independent routes:\n- codeRepo and mailArchive are reached via fileServer:lateralMovement.\n- shareMount and mailArchive are also reached via jumpHost:lateralMovement, whose parent dbLogin needs dmzWeb and tokenCache, both reachable.\n- vaultRead is reached via printServer, which is reachable from memoryDump (entries supplychain or vpnGateway) or from rdpLogin.\n\nfileServer itself has three alternative parents:\n- sshKey, which is reachable from iotDevice, containerHost or dmzWeb, each fed by multiple entries.\n- rdpLogin, which needs containerHost and tokenCache.\n- ssoLogin.\n\nChecking the key blocks:\n- Blocking fileServer leaves jumpHost to shareMount.\n- Blocking jumpHost or dbLogin leaves fileServer to codeRepo.\n- Blocking sshKey, rdpLogin or ssoLogin leaves fileServer through its other parents, and jumpHost as well.\n- Blocking memoryDump, printServer or vaultRead leaves the other collection routes.\n- Blocking any of the remaining steps also leaves at least one route."
 },
